# 5. Environment Variables

The `.env` must contain:

```env
MONGODB_URI=
JWT_SECRET=
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=
PORT=
```

Also provide:

```text
.env.example
```

Do not commit `.env` to Git.

Add `.env` to `.gitignore`.

---

# 6. User Roles

The system has these roles:

```text
CUSTOMER
STAFF
HR
ADMIN
DEFAULT_ADMIN
```

Important:

### DEFAULT_ADMIN

There must only ever be **one DEFAULT_ADMIN**.

The default admin:

- Can do everything an ADMIN can do
- Cannot be deleted
- Cannot be demoted
- Cannot be duplicated
- Cannot be created through normal account CRUD
- Must be created through a protected seed/setup process

Prevent creation of a second DEFAULT_ADMIN at the database/service level.

### ADMIN

Can:

- Manage accounts
- Manage products
- Manage categories
- Manage orders
- Manage payment options
- View dashboard
- View sales history
- Manage staff/HR/customer accounts

### STAFF

Can:

- Login to admin panel
- View dashboard
- View products
- Manage appropriate product/order operations
- View sales history
- Confirm orders
- View profile

STAFF must not manage ADMIN or DEFAULT_ADMIN accounts.

### HR

Can:

- Login to admin panel
- Manage employee/staff-related accounts according to permissions
- View profile
- Access HR-related account functionality

HR must not manage DEFAULT_ADMIN.

### CUSTOMER

Can:

- Register
- Login
- Browse products
- View product details
- Add products to cart
- Modify cart
- Place orders
- Select payment method
- Upload payment proof when required
- Use vouchers
- View order history
- Cancel eligible orders
- Download confirmed voucher
- Manage profile

---

# 7. Authentication

Use JWT authentication.

Passwords must be hashed using bcrypt.

Never store plain-text passwords.

Customer authentication and Admin authentication must be separated.

Customer login:

```text
/login
```

Admin/staff/HR login:

```text
/ecommerce-admin/login
```

Do not use the same login UI.

Admin login must reject CUSTOMER accounts.

Customer login must not provide an admin dashboard.

Use role-based middleware.

Example:

```text
authenticate
requireRole
requireAdmin
requireStaff
requireHR
```

---

# 8. Account CRUD

Implement:

```text
Create account
Read account
Read accounts with pagination
Update account
Delete account
Change role
Activate/deactivate account
```

Account roles available in admin account creation:

```text
STAFF
HR
CUSTOMER
```

Do not show DEFAULT_ADMIN in the normal role creation dropdown.

ADMIN may be available only through a protected administration mechanism.

Customer registration must always create:

```text
role = CUSTOMER
```

The customer registration form must NOT contain a role selector.

