# 44. API Layer

Frontend must NOT directly manipulate MongoDB.

Use REST APIs.

Example:

```text
GET    /api/products
GET    /api/products/:id
POST   /api/products
PUT    /api/products/:id
DELETE /api/products/:id
```

Authentication:

```text
POST /api/auth/customer/login
POST /api/auth/customer/register

POST /api/auth/admin/login
```

Orders:

```text
POST   /api/orders
GET    /api/orders
GET    /api/orders/:id
PUT    /api/orders/:id
PATCH  /api/orders/:id/status
PATCH  /api/orders/:id/cancel
```

Payments:

```text
GET  /api/payment-options
POST /api/payments
POST /api/payments/:id/proof
PATCH /api/payments/:id/verify
PATCH /api/payments/:id/reject
```

Vouchers:

```text
GET /api/vouchers
GET /api/vouchers/:id
GET /api/vouchers/:id/pdf
```

---

# 45. API Response Standard

Use consistent responses.

Success:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Product retrieved successfully",
  "data": {}
}
```

Error:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Product not found",
  "error": {
    "code": "PRODUCT_NOT_FOUND"
  }
}
```

Validation:

```json
{
  "success": false,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": [
    {
      "field": "price",
      "message": "Price must be greater than 0"
    }
  ]
}
```

---

# 46. Validation

Validate all input.

Examples:

```text
Email
Password
Product price
Stock
Quantity
Category
Order items
Payment method
Role
```

Never trust frontend validation alone.

All important validation must happen on the backend.

---

# 47. Security

Implement:

- bcrypt password hashing
- JWT authentication
- Authorization middleware
- Role-based access control
- Helmet
- CORS configuration
- Request validation
- Rate limiting for authentication endpoints
- Secure HTTP headers
- Proper error handling
- No sensitive information in error responses
- Environment variables
- File upload validation

Payment proof uploads must validate:

```text
file type
file size
```

Allow only appropriate image formats.

---

# 48. Database Design

Use MongoDB with Mongoose.

Create proper references:

```text
User
  ↓
Order
  ↓
OrderItem
  ↓
Product
```

Order should preserve product information at purchase time.

Do NOT depend entirely on the current Product document because product prices/details can change later.

OrderItem should snapshot:

```text
productId
productName
unitPrice
quantity
subtotal
```

---

# 49. Inventory Logic

When an order is created:

Do not immediately permanently remove stock unless the business logic requires reservation.

Recommended:

```text
PENDING
```

reserves stock temporarily or validates stock.

When confirmed:

```text
PENDING → CONFIRMED
```

finalize stock deduction.

When cancelled/payment failed:

restore reserved stock where applicable.

Prevent:

```text
quantity > available stock
```

---

# 50. Cart Logic

The frontend localStorage cart is only a temporary customer-side cart.

Before creating an order, the backend MUST validate:

```text
Product exists
Product active
Product available
Price
Stock
Quantity
```

Never trust price values received from localStorage.

The backend must calculate the final price using database data.

---

