# 74. Important Implementation Instruction

Do NOT build everything as one huge file.

Do NOT put:

```text
MongoDB queries
business logic
authentication
validation
response formatting
```

inside controllers.

Use:

```text
Route
 ↓
Controller
 ↓
Service
 ↓
Service Implementation
 ↓
Repository
 ↓
Model
```

Keep frontend JavaScript modular as well.

---

# 75. Final Acceptance Criteria

The project is considered complete only when:

- Customer can register
- Customer can login
- Admin can login separately
- Staff can login
- HR can login
- DEFAULT_ADMIN exists only once
- DEFAULT_ADMIN cannot be deleted
- Role-based authorization works
- Account CRUD works
- Category CRUD works
- Product CRUD works
- Payment option CRUD works
- Product pagination works
- Account pagination works
- Category pagination works
- Order pagination works
- Sales history pagination works
- Customer can browse without login
- Customer can add to cart without login
- Cart persists in localStorage
- Customer is redirected to login before checkout
- Cart survives login/register
- Customer can review order
- Customer can choose COD
- Customer can choose QR payment
- Customer can upload payment proof
- Admin can view payment proof
- Order starts as PENDING
- Staff/admin can confirm order
- Customer can cancel pending order
- Customer cannot cancel confirmed order
- Admin order modifications require reason
- Reason appears in voucher
- Voucher is generated
- PDF voucher can be downloaded after confirmation
- Failed payments are tracked
- Dashboard contains charts
- Dashboard contains last 10 orders
- All tables have pagination
- Light mode works
- Dark mode works
- Mobile responsive design works
- Animations work smoothly
- API errors are handled
- API validation works
- Every API has test cases
- Jest test suite passes
- Test coverage is generated
- README is complete
- `.env.example` exists
- Secrets are not committed
- No major console errors
- No broken API requests
- No duplicated business logic

---

# 76. Start Implementation

Start by creating the project structure and backend foundation.

Do not skip architecture.

Implement the project incrementally and keep the application runnable after each phase.

After completing each backend module:

1. Implement model
2. Implement repository
3. Implement service
4. Implement service implementation
5. Implement controller
6. Implement route
7. Implement validation
8. Implement authorization
9. Implement tests
10. Verify all tests pass

Then proceed to the next module.

Do not claim a feature is completed unless the implementation and corresponding API tests are actually present.
